+\section[Top-quark estimation]{Top-quark estimation}
+\label{sec:ch8_top}
+
+The $\ttbar$ and single-top backgrounds are constrained in the $\CRTop$ regions, which require one $\tau$ and an additional electron or muon.
+The relevant decays include $\ttbar\to b\tau\nu\,\bar b\ell\nu$ and $Wt\to b\tau\nu\,\ell\nu$.
+The additional lepton selects the second leptonic $W$ decay and separates these regions from the lepton-vetoed SRs.
+Requiring at least one tagged $b$ jet further suppresses $\wjets$ production.
+Inclusive $\ttbar$ and single-top samples are used.
+Within the $\ttbar$ and $Wt$ samples, the large-$\met$ selection favours decays in which both $W$ bosons decay leptonically.
+The top-quark purity is approximately $90\%$ after the full CR selections.
+
+The relaxed thresholds in Table~\ref{tab:ch8_top_regions} increase the CR yields.
+Single-lepton triggers permit the lower $\met>100~\GeV$ threshold.
+If more than one $b$ jet is selected, the highest-$\pT$ tagged jet defines the topology and the jet--$\tau$ observables.
+The resonant $m_{b\tau}$ requirement is removed.
