+\section{Validation regions}
+\label{sec:ch8_validation}
+
+The VRs test the prediction in selections that isolate the main changes between the CRs and SRs.
+The nominal $\VRb$ and $\VRTop$ definitions are given in Tables~\ref{tab:ch8_wcr_vrw} and~\ref{tab:ch8_top_regions}.
+Their pre-fit distributions are used to inspect the simulation before fitting, while their post-fit yields test the extrapolation of the CR constraints.
+
+\subsection[One b-jet validation with a light lepton]{One-$b$-jet validation with a light lepton}
+\label{subsec:ch8_vrw}
+
+The $\VRb$ regions retain the single-electron or single-muon final state of $\CRW$ and require exactly one tagged $b$ jet.
+The tagged jet replaces the leading untagged jet in the topology and invariant-mass selections.
+This change tests the prediction for the tagged sample, including the simulated heavy-flavour fraction of $\wjets$, before replacing the light lepton with a $\tau$ in the SR.
+The top-quark contribution increases under this selection and is predicted using the constraint from $\CRTop$.
+
+The flavour composition of vector-boson-plus-jets production depends on the kinematics and the simulation, as investigated in ATLAS modelling studies and measurements~\cite{PMGR-2021-01,STDM-2018-43,HIGG-2020-20}.
+A $30\%$ uncertainty is assigned to the ratio of $W$ production with heavy-flavour hadrons, containing $b$ or $c$ quarks, to production with light-flavour hadrons in the tagged regions.
+This uncertainty covers possible differences in the flavour composition when transferring the $b$-vetoed CR constraint to a tagged sample.
+It is treated as uncorrelated between the resonant and non-resonant categories because they select different jet-$\pT$ ranges.
+Its implementation and the remaining modelling uncertainties are described in Chapter~\ref{chapter:systematics_uncertainties}.
+
+The pre-fit $N-1$ comparisons are shown in Figures~\ref{fig:ch8_vrw_res} and~\ref{fig:ch8_vrw_nonres}.
+The electron and muon channels are combined in the plots, and their inclusive yields are listed separately in Table~\ref{tab:ch8_vrw_prefit}.
+The resonant region shows agreement within the statistical precision.
+The non-resonant region contains more data events than predicted in both lepton channels.
+The investigation of this excess and the additional check with a $\tau$ and one $b$ jet are described below.
+
