+\subsection[Top-quark validation without a light lepton]{Top-quark validation without a light lepton}
+\label{subsec:ch8_vrtop}
+
+The $\VRTop$ regions require one $\tau$, no electron or muon, and exactly two tagged $b$ jets.
+The lepton veto reproduces the SR requirement, while the second tag increases the top-quark fraction.
+The lower $\pT^\tau$ and mass thresholds in Table~\ref{tab:ch8_top_regions} provide sufficient events for the check, and $\met>200~\GeV$ keeps the selection on the $\met$-trigger plateau.
+The top-quark fractions are approximately $75\%$ and $87\%$ in the resonant and non-resonant regions, respectively.
+
+Figures~\ref{fig:ch8_vrtop_res} and~\ref{fig:ch8_vrtop_nonres} show the pre-fit $N-1$ distributions.
+The data are compatible with the simulated distributions within their statistical precision.
+Single-top production is more prominent in the resonant category, while $\ttbar$ dominates the non-resonant category.
+Together with $\VRb$, these regions test the changes in tagged-jet multiplicity and selected-lepton multiplicity on which the SR prediction depends.
+
+Signal contamination is checked using samples that include both hadronic and leptonic $\tau$ decays.
+The benchmarks are $(\MU,\gU,\beta_L^{23})=(1.5~\TeV,1.5,0.2)$ for the resonant regions and $(2.5~\TeV,1.5,1.0)$ for the non-resonant regions.
+The contamination is about $1.3\%$ and $0.7\%$ in $\VRb$, and $1.2\%$ and $0.6\%$ in $\VRTop$, respectively.
+
+\input{Chapters/background_estimation/figures_vrtop}
